  "construction": "Two-block group-algebra code C(a,b) of arXiv:2610.13880 (Table 11) over the abelian group C30 x C2 (GAP SmallGroup(60,13)): H_X = (L(a) | R(b)), H_Z = (R(b)^T | L(a)^T) with L and R the left and right regular representations, a = 1 + x^4 + x^6 y + x^11, b = 1 + x^18 y + x^25 + x^26 y in generators x (order 30) and y (order 2), i.e. the bivariate bicycle code with A = a(x,y), B = b(x,y). The stored matrices use the qubit ordering of the paper's database (record 65c01308fe794587, github.com/gideonlsx/bicycle-race @ aed705a, data/codes.jsonl, CC BY 4.0): qubits 0..59 are the left block and 60..119 the right block, group elements numbered as GAP's Elements(SmallGroup(60,13)) with e0 the identity, x = e16, y = e2, so a = e0 + e9 + e27 + e46, b = e0 + e6 + e30 + e32. Rebuilt from the database's group data; CSS commutation, k, check weight and both of the paper's witnesses were re-checked on the rebuilt matrices.",
